        <skos:definition xml:lang="en" xmlns:xml="http://www.w3.org/XML/1998/namespace">Space weather is a branch of space physics and aeronomy, or heliophysics, concerned with the time varying conditions within the Solar System, including the solar wind, emphasizing the space surrounding the Earth, including conditions in the magnetosphere, ionosphere, and thermosphere.</skos:definition>
